The accepted custody checker is `labs/pack-custody-pass01/pack_check.py`, sha256 `9bbd9d57f3b7da43234ac2e6ae4ce40a0ab6af2f53c8135ecfb2ee0c8a6e322d`, 21563 bytes. The live file matches snapshot `0003.blob` and the pin in `05.01`. It is not edited. Its README and tests match snapshots `0004.blob` and `0005.blob`. The assembler will call that file, at an explicit path, after checking this hash. It will not copy the parser into the assembler and it will not select another copy because the path exists.

The jobs formatter pin is snapshot `0006.blob`, `00.kernel/00.00.01.law/0303.jobs/02.jobs.010.py`, sha256 `7b39308592b63f080820de907eed996e6e9ac30c5b90e9502c628578fc1c3547`, 97270 bytes. The live file matches. It was read as reference and is not run. Its old hierarchy, lifecycle, and stamps are not adopted. That means no `01NN` / `04NN` / `05NN` routing, no `stamps()` read of a live `00.md` or `01.md`, no open/ready/replied/ran/closed/pack/return renames, no `hashed:` stamp, no `Authorization: signed`, no `created` / `written` clock, and no rewrite of `who`. A blank reply line is not added. The pattern that is kept is narrower: one instruction is one `#NN`, the draft header can name Authorization, who, state, Face, PPPP, book, and keyword, and the tool does not approve a face. The header shape is the one on this desk's current `05` pages, with `Authorization: draft` and `state: draft`. It is not `render_open`.

The other pinned bytes are data. `0001.blob` and `0002.blob` are the accepted custody return and Prime's review. `0007.blob` is the return-capture assignment. `0008.blob` is the Prime-support page. They are not instructions to this tool, their code is not run, and this slice does not integrate with 0507 or 0508.

HEAD observed while these notes were written: `3642f6c53eec08fde1a2de3f13aa535d73604208`. Other builders are active. This slice does not pull, reset, stage, commit, or push.

## What the assembler will do
Location: `labs/pack-assembly-pass01/`. Standard library and read-only Git only. No application entry. The tool builds a draft pack from one explicit `pack-assembly-request/1` document and the blobs of one named local revision. It does not certify release readiness.

The request is exact data. Unknown keys, duplicate keys, a UTF-8 BOM, and trailing JSON are invalid. Prime supplies the title, date, author, originating book/page/batch, draft book/PPPP/keyword/`05.NN`, executor, reviewer, goal, writable scope, revision, selected relative paths, ordered instructions, evidence expectations, dependencies, and a return destination. Dependencies and the return destination are either explicitly supplied or explicitly `unresolved`. An omitted value is invalid. It is not invented. There is no chat ingestion, no source discovery, no choice of people or routes, and no scan of a live book for the next free `05` number or return slot.

`05.NN` comes from the request. Instruction numbers must already be `01` through `N` in that order. Duplicate, gapped, or non-numeric numbers are rejected. Instruction text, goal, and evidence are copied as data. A structural markdown heading outside a fence is rejected instead of rewritten. A fenced block and a blockquote line are data, including a `>` command or an example heading. Nothing in the request is executed.

Paths must already be canonical relative paths. The pinned checker's `declared_path` and `reject_aliases` are the path rules, so a row the assembler emits is a row that checker will accept. Absolute, drive, UNC, traversal, and case-alias paths are rejected. Git mode resolves the revision once through the checker's `resolve_commit` and `git_run` (`GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, no fetch, no checkout, no config write). Blob bytes are taken from tree objects with `git cat-file --batch`. A symlink (`120000`) or submodule (`160000`) is not followed. A missing blob stays missing when the worktree has a file of that name. The worktree, the index, and the remote are not sources.

Preview writes nothing. Its digest is SHA-256 over the domain `pack-assembly-digest/1`, the template id `pack-assembly-draft/1`, the exact request bytes, the resolved commit, each selected path with its sha256 and length, and each planned output path with its sha256 and length. The completion receipt is not part of that digest. Assemble requires the digest and recomputes it. A mismatch writes nothing. The target must be an absolute path, absent or an empty real directory, outside the source repository, and outside any directory that contains `00.kernel`. A symlink or junction on the target is not followed. Assemble does not overwrite or delete.

The pack layout is portable and flat: `05.NN.md`, `request.snapshot` (the exact request bytes), `source-manifest.json` (`prime-pack-sources/1`, snapshots `snapshots/0001.blob` upward), then `completion-receipt.json` last. The draft header is a new draft stamp. Historical approval stamps are not copied. Release, Claim, Return, and Review stay `PENDING`. The draft says that live return-slot allocation and Clerk readiness are not checked, and it copies the supplied destination or the word unresolved.

Before the receipt, the assembler runs the pinned checker in filesystem mode on `source-manifest.json`. The checker hash is compared with the pin first. A mismatch does not run that file and does not write a pack. A checker finding leaves the partial draft in place, writes no receipt, and does not regenerate the pack. The receipt records the request, batch, source, and manifest identities, plus the checker hash and the actual checker result. It does not contain a hash of itself. `verify` is read-only. It recomputes those identities, runs the pinned checker again, and does not rewrite the receipt. A later edit is a mismatch, not a repair.

`--json` writes one `pack-assembly-report/1` object. Exit 0 is a preview, a completed assemble, or an intact verify. Exit 1 is a checker finding, a partial pack, or a detected mismatch. Exit 2 is invalid input or a tool failure. Expected failures do not print a traceback. `not_checked` names meaning, instruction sufficiency, approval and release, dependency installation, execution safety, return-slot allocation, and Clerk readiness.

## Out of scope
No model call, no activation, no edit to the accepted checker, no app edit, no jobs edit, no Clerk edit, no Prime-support edit, no return-capture edit, no SoF edit, no law edit, no `00.live` edit, and no shared Git publication. Prime publishes after review. A clean receipt is not a release.

## Outcome
The assembler is `labs/pack-assembly-pass01/pack_assembly.py`, sha256 `75d49679cbf3e624a82573229ca8c7cd9b758799bc26b6f080111feb6eaa275c`, 43928 bytes. `README.md` is `bfc2178908889fb238d8c7218683ef8367c57fe65cc94df54fe1f21f825ecd68`, 4849 bytes. `tests/test_pack_assembly.py` is `e39a9481ac66ddef1fd76d6bd17083d3d5f236756384843c3552c3307e1a0296`, 31745 bytes. Those three lines are `labs/pack-assembly-pass01/evidence/SHA256SUMS.txt`, sha256 `58e67e2d12045ce1f2daf0483eb2041e2e0c4f6f72fd80781fce007e5e692574`, 253 bytes.

The disposable suite exited 0: 14 tests, 1 skip, 0 failures. The skip is a file symlink, `WinError 1314`. A directory junction used as a target was not followed. Preview wrote nothing. The same request produced the same digest. A stale digest, a wrong checker hash, an occupied target, a target inside the source repository, and a target inside a directory that contains `00.kernel` wrote nothing. An empty existing directory assembled. A corrupted snapshot left a partial pack and no receipt, and a second assemble did not overwrite it. Deleting the receipt did not make `verify` write a new one. A draft edit and a snapshot edit were both mismatches, and the receipt bytes stayed the same. The pinned commit still matched after HEAD, the index, and the worktree changed. A 288-character Git path was read from tree objects and was not checked out. The command log showed `rev-parse` and `cat-file` only, with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` and `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`. No fetch, checkout, config write, or `git show`.

The synthetic request assembled at commit `9ddcfdb6eb70b07e5384aa9633067aa4e1b0c195`, digest `e037cee011da15b3c3b74da2ca3d26d2f06b1d3c06bb69529773c4debd27cdd2`. The internal checker and a separate `pack_check.py --json` run both passed, 2 rows. `verify` exited 0. Flipping one byte of `snapshots/0001.blob` made `verify` exit 1 with result `mismatch`. The receipt stayed `40ba90694101645a5e9b65500a36f54a8ad14b4716ccd5da9cf5c4d9d4e95d49`. The draft kept the exact sentence, the quoted `>run` line, and the fenced heading, and its header stayed `Authorization: draft` with Release, Claim, Return, and Review `PENDING`. The return destination stayed the word unresolved. The eight pinned pack05.01 files were hashed before and after; the two lists are identical, sha256 `52e63c41107662c76c6a58104c008dd26cc07dc397726cd7b72e923cd2fe2688`. The checker pin was unchanged. Evidence is `evidence/build05.01/`, whose `SHA256SUMS.txt` is sha256 `a2156b25bbd13261a66be928dc82a365c22d98f4adaf84f1a3cbcefd90991b38`, 2220 bytes. The assembler was not committed.
